-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      1.0 played by Jon Attree in JNext through the real loader,
              2026-11-03; 1.1 played by the owner in JNext on NextZXOS v2.10
              (System/Next 26.11), 2026-11-06: approved

  Replay      1.1: NexClash's ROM path check (nextboot.rom_paths) on the v2.10
              ROM3, 1 recording, 8591 frames: the ROM bytes the game runs or
              reads are the same as on v2.09 (1.0: BEEPER 0x03C1-0x03C4
              differs). 1.0: RZX IDENTICAL, unit PASS

  Emulator    1.1, 2026-11-06: JNext 1.1.104 headless, through the Browser and
              the real loader on System/Next 26.11 (NextZXOS v2.10) and on
              v2.09: reached play, keys answered, beeper sound in the recorded
              audio, /tmp/NEXCLASH.NEX equal to apply; 1.0 on 26.11: plays,
              but its BEEPER runs with IX never loaded. 1.0: JNext 1.1.104
              headless, through the real loader, reached play with the default
              and with Spec256 on, with Infinite lives on; frames viewed; no
              person played it; JNext 1.1.104 headless through the real
              loader, 2026-11-03: chosen in the Browser with every cheat on
              and with Enhanced, /tmp/NEXCLASH.NEX equal to apply

  Coverage    1.1 changes only the start-up stub: after its copy of the
              running ROM3 into the alt ROM it puts v2.09's bytes back at 11
              sites where that ROM3 holds v2.10's (BEEPER, PLOT, POINT, DRAW,
              CIRCLE); on v2.09 nothing changes; POINTERS (0x1664) is left as
              v2.10 has it. 1.0: Spec256 colours judged by eye in one room;
              cheats proved in a simulator on the original game: Infinite
              lives: simulator (1 player, idle): DEC (HL) at A755 runs at the
              death at frame 5182; lives 5->4 without, held at 5 with;
              Infinite bonus: simulator (idle, 7000 frames): bonus held at
              1000 with; falls 1000->0530 without; Infinite time: simulator
              (idle, 7000 frames): time held at 900 with; falls to 669
              without; Very slow big bird: simulator, level 9 (bird free),
              1500 frames: bird routine A0C8 runs 34 times with, 82 without;
              Big bird doesn't exist: simulator, level 9 (bird free), 1500
              frames: bird routine A0C8 never runs and the bird never moves
              with; 82 runs, 112 moves without; Slower hens: simulator (idle,
              7000 frames): hen-move routine 911E runs 876 times with, 2669
              without; no death with, a hen kills the player at frame 4869
              without; No hens: simulator (idle, 7000 frames): no hens on
              screen and no death with; a hen kills the player at frame 4869
              without (frames shots/nohens_compare_f2000.png)

  Hardware    untested

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
